WHAT IS A REFERENDUM:-
- Referendums are an example of direct democracy
- Used to determine public policy on one-off specific issues
- With voters choosing from a simple ‘yes’/’no’ choice on a proposal
- As decided by the government at a time of their choosing
- e.g. Brexit, Indyref, ATV referendum 2011

*****************************************************************************************************

TIMELINE OF REFERENDUMS:-
- 1975 -
    - UK to remain in EEC? (67.2% yes)
- 1979 -
    - Scottish (yes but less than 40% of electorate voted yes so ignored)
    - Wales (no)
- 1997 -
    - Scottish parliament with tax varying (yes)
    - Welsh assembly (yes)
- 1998 -
    - London mayor (yes)
    - Good Friday (yes)
- 2011 -
    - Wales primary legislative powers (yes)
    - UK AV instead of FPTP (no)
- 2014 -
    - Scottish IndyRef (no)
- 2016 -
    - Brexit (Leave wins)
    
